# Every variadic definition in this fixture. va_start reads a register save
# area the translator allocates ('__va_area__' is in the locals) and never
# fills, so selection turns the whole function away before it starts - see
# step 14 of docs/ir-codegen-design.md. Delete these lines once variadic
# definitions land; a name here that stops falling back fails the test.
vaInts
vaDoubles
vaFloats
vaMixed
vaManyBoth
vaNamedFloats
vaFiveNamed
vaSixNamed
vaNamedStruct
vaSmallArgs
vaBigArgs
vaCopied
vaNested
# 'main' is not variadic. It falls back for two reasons of its own, both step
# 13: it passes a struct larger than one register by value (to vaBigArgs and
# vaNamedStruct), which the IR passes by address while the callee reads bytes,
# and it passes a float argument on the stack, which needs a 'push xmm' that
# does not exist. The struct-returning functions it calls are selected here -
# only being variadic or passing an oversized aggregate is the problem.
main
